ose the President**: There are 8 possible people who can be chosen as the President.\n2. **Choose the Vice-President**: After the President has been chosen, there are 7 remaining people who can be chosen as the Vice-President.\n3. **Choose the Treasurer**: After the President and Vice-President have been chosen, there are 6 remaining people who can be chosen as the Treasurer.\n\nWe multiply the number of choices for each position to find the total number of ways to choose the President, Vice-President, and Treasurer:\n\n\\[\n8 \\times 7 \\times 6 = 336\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of ways to choose a President, Vice-President, and Treasurer from a group of 8 people is \\(\\boxed{336}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{336}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:80"}
